  "bookId": "2CO",
  "reference": "2 Corinthians 6",
  "verseCount": 16,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "6",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "2CO 6"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "6",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In our work together with God, then, we beg you who have received God's grace not to let it be wasted. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "ISA.49.8"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Is 49.8",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hear what God says:",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.2"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "We do not want anyone to find fault with our work, so we try not to put obstacles in anyone's way. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Instead, in everything we do we show that we are God's servants by patiently enduring troubles, hardships, and difficulties. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "ACT.16.23"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Acts 16.23",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "We have been beaten, imprisoned, and mobbed; we have been overworked and have gone without sleep or food. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "By our purity, knowledge, patience, and kindness we have shown ourselves to be God's servants — by the Holy Spirit, by our true love, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "by our message of truth, and by the power of God. We have righteousness as our weapon, both to attack and to defend ourselves. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "We are honoured and disgraced; we are insulted and praised. We are treated as liars, yet we speak the truth; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "as unknown, yet we are known by all; as though we were dead, but, as you see, we live on. Although punished, we are not killed; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "although saddened, we are always glad; we seem poor, but we make many people rich; we seem to have nothing, yet we really possess everything.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.10"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Dear friends in Corinth! We have spoken frankly to you; we have opened our hearts wide. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "It is not we who have closed our hearts to you; it is you who have closed your hearts to us. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I speak now as though you were my children: show us the same feelings that we have for you. Open your hearts wide!",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.13"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Do not try to work together as equals with unbelievers, for it cannot be done. How can right and wrong be partners? How can light and darkness live together? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "How can Christ and the Devil agree? What does a believer have in common with an unbeliever? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CO 6:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "LEV.26.12"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Lev 26.12",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "EZK.37.27"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ezek 37.27",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1CO.3.16"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "1 Cor 3.16",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1CO.6.19"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "6.19",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "How can God's temple come to terms with pagan idols? For we are the temple of the living God! As God himself has said:",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CO.6.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CO.6.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
